1497	// markers plus one `cfg!(feature = "k3")` block inside `main`.
1498	//
1499	// Three tiers, first one that works wins:
1500	//   1. generate — run the generator with a build-host Python that has the
1501	//      pinned TileLang. Preferred; this is what a dev box and the GPU CI
1502	//      builders take.
1503	//   2. pre-generated — `PEGAINFER_K3_TILELANG_PREGEN=<dir>` points at a
1504	//      directory produced earlier by `generate.py --vendor-includes`, for
1505	//      hosts that cannot install TileLang. The directory carries its own
1506	//      `manifest.txt` with the CUDA files and header include paths.
1507	//   3. stub — no Python, no pre-generated dir: compile launchers that return
1508	//      `cudaErrorNotSupported`, so a featureless/CI build stays green and a
1509	//      K3 decode attempt fails loudly instead of silently computing garbage.
1510	// ===========================================================================
